  "source_caveat": "Both original Census employer industry revenue and BEA gross output are current-dollar U.S. trucking NAICS 484 economic statistics but not identical definitions or necessarily identical establishments or service-weighted populations. BEA gross output is a gross-industry-production-account concept that can include transactions and intermediate activity not counted identically by Census employer establishment revenue. The dollar differences, ratios and relative growth rates from 2017 to 2024 can be computed, but cannot be causally decomposed without independent BEA/Census source methodology and establishment coverage crosswalk. These differences are NOT missing freight invoices, recoverable bill overcharges, a share of carrier payments, addressable audit market, actual refunds or customer demand. BLS industry net-output producer price index annual means and BEA gross-output prices are differently scoped price measures; a numerically similar price change cannot validate a common denominator. BEA parent industry 484 includes TL 484121 and LTL 484122, so parent plus children are not additive. M29, M25, M33 original source lineages remain separate, and all 18 independent real customer pilot evidence approvals remain unmet."
